00:01:30.343 --> 00:01:37.824
<v MAN> Excuse me. Would you mind if I asked you some questions? We're doing a survey on transport.

00:01:37.826 --> 00:01:39.824
<v SADIE> Yes, that's OK.

00:01:39.825 --> 00:01:42.452
<v MAN> First of all, can I take your name?

00:01:42.454 --> 00:01:45.425
<v SADIE> Yes. It's Sadie Jones.

00:01:45.426 --> 00:01:52.654
<v MAN> Thanks very much. And could I have your date of birth – just the year will do, actually. Is that all right?

00:01:52.656 --> 00:01:57.760
<v SADIE> Yes, that's fine. It's 1991.

00:01:57.761 --> 00:02:01.246
<v MAN> So next your postcode, please.

00:02:01.248 --> 00:02:07.632
<v SADIE> It's DW30 7YZ.

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:11.097
<v MAN> Great. Thanks. Is that in Wells?

00:02:11.098 --> 00:02:16.310
<v SADIE> No it's actually in Harborne – Wells isn't far from there, though.

00:02:16.311 --> 00:02:21.212
<v MAN> I really like that area. My grandmother lived there when I was a kid.

00:02:21.213 --> 00:02:23.446
<v SADIE> Yes, it is nice.

00:02:23.448 --> 00:02:32.132
<v MAN> Right, so now I want to ask you some questions about how you travelled here today. Did you use public transport?

00:02:32.134 --> 00:02:34.702
<v SADIE> Yes. I came by bus.

00:02:34.704 --> 00:02:40.822
<v MAN> OK. And that was today. It's the 24th of April, isn't it?

00:02:40.823 --> 00:02:46.400
<v SADIE> Isn't it the 25th? No, actually, you're right.

00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:53.290
<v MAN> Ha ha. And what was the reason for your trip today? I can see you've got some shopping with you.

00:02:53.291 --> 00:03:00.697
<v SADIE> Yes. I did some shopping but the main reason I came here was to go to the dentist.

00:03:00.699 --> 00:03:04.395
<v MAN> That's not much fun. Hope it was nothing serious.

00:03:04.396 --> 00:03:07.771
<v SADIE> No, it was just a check-up. It's fine.

00:03:07.772 --> 00:03:11.942
<v MAN> Good. Do you normally travel by bus into the city centre?

00:03:11.943 --> 00:03:21.527
<v SADIE> Yes. I stopped driving in ages ago because parking was so difficult to find and it costs so much.

00:03:21.529 --> 00:03:22.573
<v MAN> I see.

00:03:22.575 --> 00:03:28.002
<v SADIE> The bus is much more convenient too. It only takes about 30 minutes.

00:03:28.003 --> 00:03:31.614
<v MAN> That's good. So where did you start your journey?

00:03:31.615 --> 00:03:35.608
<v SADIE> At the bus stop on Claxby Street.

00:03:35.609 --> 00:03:40.045
<v MAN> Is that C-L-A-X-B-Y?

00:03:40.047 --> 00:03:41.074
<v SADIE> That's right.

00:04:21.165 --> 00:04:26.181
<v MAN> And how satisfied with the service are you? Do you have any complaints?

00:04:26.182 --> 00:04:38.515
<v SADIE> Well, as I said, it's very convenient and quick when it's on time, but this morning it was late. Only about 10 minutes, but still.

00:04:38.517 --> 00:04:45.274
<v MAN> Yes, I understand that's annoying. And what about the timetable? Do you have any comments about that?

00:04:45.275 --> 00:05:03.583
<v SADIE> Mmm. I suppose I mainly use the bus during the day, but any time I've been in town in the evening – for dinner or at the cinema – I've noticed you have to wait a long time for a bus – there aren't that many.

00:05:03.585 --> 00:05:09.036
<v MAN> OK, thanks. So now I'd like to ask you about your car use.

00:05:09.038 --> 00:05:23.938
<v SADIE> Well, I have got a car but I don't use it that often. Mainly just to go to the supermarket. But that's about it really. My husband uses it at the weekends to go to the golf club.

00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:25.619
<v MAN> And what about a bicycle?

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.309
<v SADIE> I don't actually have one at the moment.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:32.434
<v MAN> What about the city bikes you can rent? Do you ever use those?

00:05:32.436 --> 00:05:43.160
<v SADIE> No – I'm not keen on cycling there because of all the pollution. But I would like to get a bike – it would be good to use it to get to work.

00:05:43.162 --> 00:05:45.477
<v MAN> So why haven't you got one now?

00:05:45.479 --> 00:05:56.508
<v SADIE> Well, I live in a flat – on the second floor and it doesn't have any storage – so we'd have to leave it in the hall outside the flat.

00:05:56.509 --> 00:06:01.294
<v MAN> I see. OK. Well, I think that's all …